.policy "ruff-d101-undocumented-public-class" revision 2
.description "Give each public Python class a docstring that explains what it represents and how to use it."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff D101 (pydocstyle): a public module-level class with no docstring. Public: the module is (no `_x` segment
// in its name), the class is listed in `__all__` when there is one, and its name does not start with `_`.
// `.pyi` stubs are not checked.
//   class Widget:              ← D101 at `Widget`
//       x = 1
//   class _Private: ...        not reported
#include "python/docstrings.rr"

.violation D101(at: node, x: symbol) code "D101"
    "Add a docstring as the first statement of class `{x}`, explaining what it represents and how to use it."
    suppress ruff "D101"
D101(nm, x) :- doc_missing(_, "class", nm, x).